<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guruuswa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guruuswa was a southern province of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa</a> state on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwean plateau</a>. Around 1670 the Mutapa ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mukombwe">Mukombwe</a> granted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/changamire-dombo">Changamire Dombo I</a> herds and authority there. Dombo used this base to build a loyal military following, from which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rozvi-empire">Rozvi Empire</a> emerged.</p></div>
